  "user_handle": "YouCrossTheLineAlfie",
  "body": "## Finding description\n\nThe [`PanopticVaultAccountant::computeNAV`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-06-panoptic/blob/8ef6d867a5fb6ffd1a6cc479a2380a611d452b4a/src/accountants/PanopticVaultAccountant.sol#L94) is used in order to compute the NAV of the portfolio contained in `vault` in terms of its underlying token (which considers the balance of underlying tokens present in the vault as well).\n\nThis is used inside the [`HypoVault::fulfillDeposits`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-06-panoptic/blob/8ef6d867a5fb6ffd1a6cc479a2380a611d452b4a/src/HypoVault.sol#L472) and [`HypoVault::fulfillWithdrawals`](https://github.com/code-423n4/2025-06-panoptic/blob/8ef6d867a5fb6ffd1a6cc479a2380a611d452b4a/src/HypoVault.sol#L516) to calculte the total assets, calculate the shares and update the total supply accordingly:\n```solidity\n    function fulfillDeposits(\n        uint256 assetsToFulfill,\n        bytes memory managerInput\n    ) external onlyManager {\n        uint256 currentEpoch = depositEpoch;\n\n        DepositEpochState memory epochState = depositEpochState[currentEpoch];\n\n        uint256 totalAssets = accountant.computeNAV(address(this), underlyingToken, managerInput) +                         <<@\n            1 -\n            epochState.assetsDeposited -\n            reservedWithdrawalAssets;\n\n        uint256 _totalSupply = totalSupply;\n\n        uint256 sharesReceived = Math.mulDiv(assetsToFulfill, _totalSupply, totalAssets);                                   <<@\n\n        uint256 assetsRemaining = epochState.assetsDeposited - assetsToFulfill;\n\n        depositEpochState[currentEpoch] = DepositEpochState({\n            assetsDeposited: uint128(epochState.assetsDeposited),\n            sharesReceived: uint128(sharesReceived),\n            assetsFulfilled: uint128(assetsToFulfill)\n        });\n\n        currentEpoch++;\n        depositEpoch = uint128(currentEpoch);\n\n        depositEpochState[currentEpoch] = DepositEpochState({\n            assetsDeposited: uint128(assetsRemaining),\n            sharesReceived: 0,\n            assetsFulfilled: 0\n        });\n\n        totalSupply = _totalSupply + sharesReceived;                                                                        <<@\n\n        emit DepositsFulfilled(currentEpoch, assetsToFulfill, sharesReceived);\n    }\n```\n\n```solidity\n function fulfillWithdrawals(\n        uint256 sharesToFulfill,\n        uint256 maxAssetsReceived,\n        bytes memory managerInput\n    ) external onlyManager {\n        uint256 _reservedWithdrawalAssets = reservedWithdrawalAssets;\n        uint256 totalAssets = accountant.computeNAV(address(this), underlyingToken, managerInput) +                         <<@\n            1 -\n            depositEpochState[depositEpoch].assetsDeposited -\n            _reservedWithdrawalAssets;\n\n        uint256 currentEpoch = withdrawalEpoch;\n\n        WithdrawalEpochState memory epochState = withdrawalEpochState[currentEpoch];\n\n        uint256 _totalSupply = totalSupply;\n\n        uint256 assetsReceived = Math.mulDiv(sharesToFulfill, totalAssets, _totalSupply);\n\n        if (assetsReceived > maxAssetsReceived) revert WithdrawalNotFulfillable();\n\n        uint256 sharesRemaining = epochState.sharesWithdrawn - sharesToFulfill;\n\n        withdrawalEpochState[currentEpoch] = WithdrawalEpochState({\n            assetsReceived: uint128(assetsReceived),\n            sharesWithdrawn: uint128(epochState.sharesWithdrawn),\n            sharesFulfilled: uint128(sharesToFulfill)                                           <<@\n        });\n\n        currentEpoch++;\n\n        withdrawalEpoch = uint128(currentEpoch);\n\n        withdrawalEpochState[currentEpoch] = WithdrawalEpochState({\n            assetsReceived: 0,\n            sharesWithdrawn: uint128(sharesRemaining),\n            sharesFulfilled: 0\n        });\n\n        totalSupply = _totalSupply - sharesToFulfill;                                           <<@\n\n        reservedWithdrawalAssets = _reservedWithdrawalAssets + assetsReceived;\n\n        emit WithdrawalsFulfilled(currentEpoch, assetsReceived, sharesToFulfill);\n    }\n```\n\nHowever, directly reading the contract's underlying balance will lead to serious consequences:\n\n1. First ever `fulfillDeposits` will naturally have `totalAssets` to be calculated as 1 as there are no funds deposited / managed yet.\n```solidity\nuint256 totalAssets = accountant.computeNAV(address(this), underlyingToken, managerInput) +\n            1 -\n            epochState.assetsDeposited -\n            reservedWithdrawalAssets;\n            // Returns 1\n```\nThis can be confirmed from the tests as well where it clearly shows `totalAssets` being 1 as well as if we apply common sense.\n\n2. However, if an attacker frontruns the `fulfillDeposits` call and donates `underlyingToken` here, it would change the `sharesReceived` drastically: \n```solidity\n    uint256 sharesReceived = Math.mulDiv(assetsToFulfill, _totalSupply, totalAssets);\n\n    // Ideal Case\n    // total assets would be 1\n    // assetsToFulFill is scaled to 18 decimals and _totalSupply is initially set to 1e6\n    // Hence final decimals of the sharesReceived would be 24 \n\n    // Malicious Case\n    // Attacker donates an arbitrary amount of underlying to the vault, preferrably >= assetsToFulfill\n    // Fair to assume sharesReceived would be around <= 6 digit.\n```\n\n3. As `sharesReceived` are calculated to be with 6 decimals, it would not increase the `totalSupply` much.\n```solidity\n        totalSupply = _totalSupply + sharesReceived;\n```\nHowever, the ideal scaling which we would've achieved without donation is now missing and will always stay missing as the denominator is now no longer 1.\n\nHence, everytime a deposit arrives, the shares received calculation would be scaled similarly:\n```solidity\n        uint256 totalAssets = accountant.computeNAV(address(this), underlyingToken, managerInput) +\n            1 -\n            epochState.assetsDeposited -\n            reservedWithdrawalAssets;\n\n        uint256 _totalSupply = totalSupply;\n\n        uint256 sharesReceived = Math.mulDiv(assetsToFulfill, _totalSupply, totalAssets);       <<@ // (18 dec * 6 dec) / 18 decimals\n```\n\nAs total assets keep increasing, a point would arrive where `assetsToFulfill * _totalSupply` < `totalAssets`.\nThis would lead to `0` sharesReceived.\n\n```solidity\n        depositEpochState[currentEpoch] = DepositEpochState({\n            assetsDeposited: uint128(epochState.assetsDeposited),\n            sharesReceived: uint128(sharesReceived),            <<@\n            assetsFulfilled: uint128(assetsToFulfill)\n        });\n```\n\nThis would not allow deposits to mint any shares:\n\n```solidity\n    function executeDeposit(address user, uint256 epoch) external {\n        if (epoch >= depositEpoch) revert EpochNotFulfilled();\n\n        uint256 queuedDepositAmount = queuedDeposit[user][epoch];\n        queuedDeposit[user][epoch] = 0;\n\n        DepositEpochState memory _depositEpochState = depositEpochState[epoch];\n\n        uint256 userAssetsDeposited = Math.mulDiv(\n            queuedDepositAmount,\n            _depositEpochState.assetsFulfilled,\n            _depositEpochState.assetsDeposited\n        );\n\n        uint256 sharesReceived = Math.mulDiv(\n            userAssetsDeposited,\n            _depositEpochState.sharesReceived,                          <<@ -- // 0\n            _depositEpochState.assetsFulfilled\n        );\n\n        // shares from pending deposits are already added to the supply at the start of every new epoch\n        _mintVirtual(user, sharesReceived);                             <<@ // 0 Mint\n```\n\n\nHence, we would see unprecedented loss of funds here.\n\n\n\n\nBONUS FACTOR:\nOne more thing to consider here is that the amount donated is not fully lost, we can consider the donated amount to being proportionately split between the users:\n```solidity\n    function fulfillWithdrawals(\n        uint256 sharesToFulfill,\n        uint256 maxAssetsReceived,\n        bytes memory managerInput\n    ) external onlyManager {\n        uint256 _reservedWithdrawalAssets = reservedWithdrawalAssets;\n        uint256 totalAssets = accountant.computeNAV(address(this), underlyingToken, managerInput) +\n            1 -\n            depositEpochState[depositEpoch].assetsDeposited -\n            _reservedWithdrawalAssets;\n\n        uint256 currentEpoch = withdrawalEpoch;\n\n        WithdrawalEpochState memory epochState = withdrawalEpochState[currentEpoch];\n\n        uint256 _totalSupply = totalSupply;\n\n        uint256 assetsReceived = Math.mulDiv(sharesToFulfill, totalAssets, _totalSupply);           <<@  -- // Will be higher than ideal case\n```\n\nThe `assetsReceived` here would be higher as the `totalAssets` is inflated in nature due to donated funds.\n\nAn attacker can simply use the next epoch's `fulfillDeposits` with a very huge deposit, this would allow the attacker to request a withdrawal right before fulfilling withdrawals in the next epoch ( this can be frontran as well ).\n\nHence, allowing attacker to regain back some of his funds.\n\n\n## Impact\n\n1. The intended scaling of shares will get broken beyond repair irrespective of the deciamals of the underlying (attack above works for both 18 and 6 decimal ~ USDT / USDC tokens).\n2. Loss of funds over several epochs.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nIt is recommended to instead include a scaling factor rather than relying on the initial value's scaling.",
  "proof_of_concept": "Add the following test case inside `HypoVault.t.sol`:\n\n```solidity\n    function test_donation_affecting_shares_decimals() public {\n\n        // Deposit amount\n        uint256 depositAmount = 50 ether;\n\n        // Request deposit\n        vm.prank(Alice);\n        vault.requestDeposit(uint128(depositAmount));\n\n        \n        uint256 totalSupplyBefore = vault.totalSupply();\n        uint256 totalAssets = depositAmount + 1 - depositAmount - vault.reservedWithdrawalAssets(); // = 1\n        // Calculate expected shares\n        uint256 expectedShares = calculateExpectedShares(\n            depositAmount,\n            totalAssets,\n            totalSupplyBefore\n        );\n        console.log(depositAmount, totalAssets, totalSupplyBefore);\n        console.log(\"ExpectedShares: \", expectedShares);\n        assertEq(totalAssets, 1);\n\n        // Simulating donation of `depositAmount` equivalent\n        totalAssets = depositAmount * 2 + 1 - depositAmount - vault.reservedWithdrawalAssets();\n\n        assertEq(totalAssets, 50000000000000000001);\n        \n        // Simulating new expected shares\n        uint newExpectedShares = calculateExpectedShares(\n            depositAmount,\n            totalAssets,\n            totalSupplyBefore\n        );\n\n        assertNotEq(newExpectedShares, expectedShares);\n\n        // Contrast difference can be seen here with scaling\n        assertEq(expectedShares, 50000000000000000000000000);\n        assertEq(newExpectedShares, 999999);\n\n    }\n```",
